      <div type="clause" n="13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 13</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>LVII. Gif hwa beforan biscepe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_13.lnote.oe.13"/> his gewitnesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_13.lnote.oe.14"/> ⁊ his wed aleoge, gebete mid CXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_13.lnote.oe.15"/> scill.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>LVII. . . . beforan biscope his gewitnesse ⁊ his wed aleoge, gebete mid hundtwelftigum scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="94" ed="#liebermann"/>LVII. Gif hwa beforan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_13.lnote.oe.8"/> biscope his<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_13.lnote.oe.6"/> gewitnesse ⁊ his wed<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_13.lnote.oe.9"/> aleoge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_13.lnote.oe.10"/>, gebete mid CXX scillingum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>Be þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe heore gewitnesse geleogað. Gyf hwá beforan bisceope his gewitnysse ⁊ his wed aleoge, gebete mid hundtwelftig scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="13" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_13.lnote.oe.17"/> coram episcopo testimonium suum et uadium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_13.lnote.oe.18"/> mentiatur, centum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_13.lnote.oe.19"/> uiginti solid. emendet.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="40" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be þam þe heore gewitnesse geleogað.] Gif hwa beforan biscepe his gewitnesse ⁊ his wed aleoge, gebete mid CXX scill.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="13" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="378" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LVII} Gif hwa biforan biscepe his gewitnesse ⁊ his wed aleoge, gebete mid CXX sciƚƚ.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="95" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand vor dem Bischofe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_13.lnote.de.1"/> sein Zeugniss falsch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_13.lnote.de.2"/> abgiebt und sein rechtsförmliches Versprechen [abgegeben vor ihm,] bricht, büsse er mit 120 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_13.lnote.de.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone gives false testimony before the bishop and breaks his formal pledge [given before him], let him pay 120 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="41" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone bears false witness in the presence of a bishop, or repudiates a pledge which he has given in his presence, he shall pay 120 shillings compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="401" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone in the bishop’s presence bears false witness and breaks his pledge, he is to pay 120 shillings compensation.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="379" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone gives false witness or denies his pledge before the bishop, let him compensate with 120 shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>gloss to</label> <ref target="clause:Af_22">Af 22</ref> <quote>Up to forty ... items ... look like glosses to Ine (n. 78: add Af 22 compared to Ine 8 (or 13, 35:1, 75))</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt RT</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in RT</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ponat et <hi rend="italic">fügt zu übergeschr. Co; im Texte Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ponat et added above the line by Co; in the text in Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">95</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XXX <hi rend="italic">MHkBr;</hi> VII <hi rend="italic">Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XXX MHkBr; VII Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> wedd</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to wedd</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eo <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eo on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ceope <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ceope Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nysse <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nysse Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">94</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hundtwelftig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hundtwelftig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Meineid 2a. 12; Eidesform 5a. 7h; Zeugen 5. d. Keineswegs Geistliches Gericht, sondern nur die Teilnahme Geistlicher an der Abnahme von Eid und Versprechen (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 6), die Einwirkung des Kirchenstaatsrechts (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 17) darauf, folgt hieraus. Für Meineid <hi rend="italic">in manu episcopi</hi> diktiert 3 Jahre Kirchenbusse Theodor <hi rend="italic">Poenit.</hi> II 6, 3f. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Ungehorsam 15</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Meineid 2a. 12; Eidesform 5a. 7h; Zeugen 5. d. What follows from this is by no means an ecclesiastical court, but only the participation of clergy in the taking of oaths and pledges (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 6) and the influence of ecclesiastical public law (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 17) on it. For perjury <hi rend="italic">in manu episcopi</hi> Theodore <hi rend="italic">Poenit.</hi> II 6, 3f. prescribes 3 years of ecclesiastical penance. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Ungehorsam 15</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aleogan:</hi> ‘assertorisch oder promissorisch falsch sprechen’; <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Af 1, 1⁴</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">aleogan:</hi> ‘to speak falsely, assertorily or promissorily’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Af 1, 1⁴</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_13.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">70</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Grosshundert, während ‘½ Wergeld = 100 Schill.’ II Cn 36 fordert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Long hundred, whereas II Cn 36 demands ‘½ wergild = 100 shill.’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_13.attnote.n.0" n="0" source="#attenborough" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">This clause curiously breaks the connection between cap. 12 and 13 § 1.</seg></note>
      </div>
